  "passageOverrides": [],
  "correctionOfR7": "r7 §4.3's sentence \"The only build the guard newly refuses is `--release --features scenario-fixtures` on security\" holds for its measured non-test matrix. `--release --tests` on storage and lifecycle is also refused, because their dev-dependencies enable the fixture feature, which is what the guard is for (evidence guard-release-tests-v1 in the unit's cache, measured at product bcd03cd; LD-Q-257). The adopted text must not be read as exhaustive. No code change and no separate erratum.",
  "section45": "The security-completion.v2 §4.5 contract successor is NOT published here. It is discharged by SEC-HARDEN-1's binding, naming all four consumers (P-1, X4T admission, X4B acceptance, the X4 observer), per SUCCESSOR-SECHARDEN-RELEASE r2 line 28 and LD-Q-261, which corrects LD-Q-260. Until then the adopted COMPONENT-RELEASE-SUBJECT and SECHARDEN records govern, and P-1 implements them.",
